# NOAA CO-OPS Data Retrieval API response (format=json): station metadata and a list of
# observations, or a list of tide predictions, or an error. Public (US Government work).
# Written by hand from the API's documented response columns; every value is text, as the
# API sends it. pack.md states what is mapped and why nothing is bound to a shared key.
format  coops-data
version 0.1.0
distribution public
source  "NOAA CO-OPS Data Retrieval API, https://api.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/api/prod/ (page sha256 2f35c273fdb3eeca2aa98111d0ed62998500c2ed9f4c507b0543d919dd6b4da5), and its Response Help page, https://api.tidesandcurrents.noaa.gov/api/prod/responseHelp.html (sha256 c934a7921f56b80bbd5b05701795357a97cb5cb3c692931c3d96e8194976ba69), read 2026-11-20"
uses    coops
wire    json

kind    observations
when    data  present
requires coops.data
field   coops.station_id    metadata.id    string
field   coops.station_name  metadata.name  string
field   coops.station_lat   metadata.lat   string
field   coops.station_lon   metadata.lon   string
group   coops.data  data
  field  coops.t   t   string
  field  coops.v   v   string
  field  coops.s   s   string
  field  coops.d   d   string
  field  coops.dr  dr  string
  field  coops.g   g   string
  field  coops.ty  ty  string
  field  coops.f   f   string
  field  coops.q   q   string
end

kind    predictions
when    predictions  present
requires coops.predictions
group   coops.predictions  predictions
  field  coops.t     t     string
  field  coops.v     v     string
end

kind    error
when    error.message  present
requires coops.error_message
field   coops.error_message  error.message  string
